# iGRYT Event Timer — storage configuration
#
# THE DEFAULT IS localStorage. With no .env file at all the app runs fully
# offline: no network, no account, no Supabase code paths. That is the supported
# race-day configuration unless you deliberately opt into Supabase.
#
# ── Opting into Supabase ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in BOTH values below with real project
# credentials (Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API). Supabase activates
# only when both are present and well-formed; blank, partial, or still-templated
# values keep the app on localStorage instead of half-configuring it.
#
# In Supabase mode organizers must sign in (RLS keys every write to the owner's
# identity). Enable Email auth under Authentication → Providers; turning off
# "Confirm email" gives the quickest local loop. Apply
# supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql before first use. See the README.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Explicit backend override (optional) ────────────────────────────────────
# Leave unset for auto-detection (Supabase if the credentials above are usable,
# otherwise localStorage).
#
#   local     — force localStorage even when credentials are present. This is the
#               race-day escape hatch back to a known-good offline app.
#   supabase  — require Supabase. If the credentials are missing or malformed the
#               app still falls back to localStorage rather than breaking, and
#               shows a "Local only" warning explaining why.
#
# VITE_STORAGE_BACKEND=local
